What is the ancestry of Elisabeth, Countess Of Vermandois?
Elisabeth, Countess of Vermandois, is the daughter of Ralph I, Count of Vermandois, and his second spouse Petronilla of Aquitaine. Her ancestry includes:

* Paternal grandfather: Herbert IV of Vermandois (Carolingian ancestry)
* Maternal grandfather: William IX, Duke of Aquitaine (Aquitaine ancestry)
* Maternal grandmother: Philippa of Toulouse (Toulouse ancestry)
* Maternal great-grandmother: Emma of Anjou (Anjou ancestry)
* Maternal great-great-grandmother: Agnes of Burgundy (Burgundy ancestry)

Additionally, Elisabeth is the first cousin of Richard I of England and John of England, as her mother Petronilla is the sister of Eleanor of Aquitaine, Queen consort of both France and England.
